  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Widespread soaking rain expected Thursday. Some\ndrought relief is possible, though flooding is not expected.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nHigh pressure exits across the Maritimes Wednesday night while \nan occluded front approaches from the west. An area of rain will\nbegin to expand eastward across the forecast area Wednesday \nnight in advance of the front. A disturbance moving around an \nupper low across Quebec province will help support a developing \nlow along the front Thursday. Rain will occur regionwide \nThursday. The developing low will begin to cross the Gulf of \nMaine Thursday night, though the exact track is still uncertain.\nRain chances will begin to diminish later Thursday night. The \nsurface low exits across the Maritimes Friday, while the upper \nlow crosses the region. Showers will persist across the region \nFriday, with the better chances across northern areas. The \nsurface/upper lows vertically stack across the Maritimes Friday \nnight into Saturday, slowing the movement of the system. Shower \nchances will persist Friday night into Saturday. The system then\nexits Saturday night into Sunday. The entire forecast area \nshould receive a soaking rain Later Wednesday night into \nThursday night. Rainfall totals exceeding 1 inch are between 30% \nand 50%, although those chances have diminished slightly. \nGenerally higher totals are expected in the South, but will \ndepend on where the low sets up in the Gulf of Maine.",
